{
  "id": "Lyo.Web.Host",
  "name": "Lyo.Web.Host",
  "area": "Apps",
  "tagline": "Shared Blazor host shell so a second app does not have to copy TestGateway's layout, theme, and client DI.",
  "description": "App bar, drawer, dark-mode toggle, reconnect modal, and `AddLyoWebShell()` for the client-side services every Lyo Blazor host needs. The host still owns auth and domain navigation through render fragments. TestGateway now wraps `LyoAppShell` instead of owning the chrome.",
  "features": [
    "MudBlazor providers, the drawer, the app bar, and the theme toggle (saved through `ClientStore`) all sit on `LyoAppShell`.",
    "One `AddLyoWebShell` call registers MudBlazor, local storage, `IJsInterop`, `ILyoTimeZone`, `ClientStore`, status palettes, and the workbench registry.",
    "`LyoReconnectModal` is the circuit reconnect dialog, lifted out of TestGateway so every host shares the same recovery UI."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Wire up the shell",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "builder.Services.AddLyoWebShell();\nbuilder.Services.AddLyoScheduleWorkbench();"
    }
  ],
